lesson.fix:
Add authentication (e.g., API key or admin token) to the client‑registration endpoint so only trusted parties can create clients. Validate each supplied redirect_uri against a whitelist of allowed domains and enforce HTTPS. Reject URLs that contain IP addresses, localhost, or unknown hosts. When processing redirect_uri, compare it to the stored whitelist and return an error if it does not match. Example fix in pseudo‑code:

```python
if not user_is_authorized(request):
    return 403
for uri in data["redirect_uris"]:
    if not is_allowed_uri(uri):
        return 400
store_client(data)
```
This prevents open redirects and stops the server from fetching attacker‑controlled URLs, eliminating the SSRF vector.
